Associate Director,Social &lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About WPP Media&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands. With exceptional talent, trusted data and intelligence, and world-class partnerships – all united by our pioneering agentic marketing platform, WPP Open – we help clients navigate change, capture opportunity, and deliver transformational growth. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WPP Media is WPP&#39;s AI-driven media operating unit, bringing together media, data, and partnerships to deliver creative personalisation at scale. Connected through WPP Open and powered by Open Intelligence, clients see exactly where, how, and why their media investment is working.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For more information, visit &lt;a href=&quot;wppmedia.com&quot;&gt;wppmedia.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2480 - Associate Director, Social&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Summary and Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Paid Social Account Director, you will be pivotal in ensuring the successful execution and optimisation of paid social campaigns across your assigned client accounts. This role requires a strong blend of hands-on paid social expertise, meticulous campaign management, and effective team leadership. You will be responsible for overseeing the day-to-day paid social output, ensuring campaigns align with client objectives and deliver measurable results. Cultivating strong client relationships will be key, acting as a primary point of contact and trusted advisor. You will also mentor and develop a team of social specialists, fostering their growth and ensuring innovative, high-quality campaign delivery that maximises client ROI across all relevant social channels. Ultimately, you will contribute significantly to client success and the agency&#39;s reputation through expert delivery and stakeholder management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills and Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At WPP Media, we believe in the power of our culture and our people. It’s what elevates us to deliver exceptional experiences for both our clients and each other. In this role it will be critical to embrace WPP &amp;amp; WPP Media’s shared core values:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be &lt;strong&gt;Extraordinary&lt;/strong&gt; by &lt;em&gt;Leading Collectively&lt;/em&gt; to &lt;em&gt;Inspire transformational Creativity.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create an &lt;strong&gt;Open&lt;/strong&gt; environment by&lt;em&gt; Balancing People and Client Experiences&lt;/em&gt; by &lt;em&gt;Cultivating Trust&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead &lt;strong&gt;Optimistically&lt;/strong&gt; by &lt;em&gt;Championing Growth&lt;/em&gt; &lt;em&gt;and Development&lt;/em&gt; to &lt;em&gt;Mobilize the Enterprise&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills &amp;amp; Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Account Directors are charged with responsibility for the day-to-day paid social output of one (or more) client accounts, with several key areas of focus. These include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Extensive Paid Social Expertise:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;In-depth, hands-on proficiency across all major paid social advertising platforms, including Meta Ads Manager (essential) plus TikTok Ads Manager and Pinterest Ads Manager (desired). Minimum of 4+ years of experience in paid social media.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Supervision &amp;amp; Development:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Proven track record of successfully overseeing, mentoring, and developing a team of junior paid social specialists. This includes guiding day-to-day account management, ensuring performance standards, and fostering professional growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client &amp;amp; Stakeholder Management:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Demonstrable ability to build and maintain strong client relationships, serving as a trusted point of contact and advisor. Capable of developing and nurturing relationships with suppliers and other internal/external stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial Acumen &amp;amp; Strategic Execution:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Strong understanding of how paid social campaigns contribute to business objectives and ROI. Ability to translate client goals into effective campaign strategies and oversee their successful execution, including budget management and identifying optimisation opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical &amp;amp; Reporting Excellence:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Proficient in interpreting complex campaign data, identifying key trends, deriving actionable insights, and presenting comprehensive performance reports and recommendations to stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication &amp;amp; Presentation:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to articulate complex strategies and performance insights clearly, concisely, and persuasively to diverse audiences. Confident in leading client calls and presentations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Project &amp;amp; Quality Management:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Excellent organisational skills, adept at managing multiple client projects and team priorities concurrently, ensuring adherence to quality standards and best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Skills &amp;amp; Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of contributing to new business pitches and client growth initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant industry certifications (e.g., Meta Blueprint).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Life at WPP Media &amp;amp; Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our passion for shaping the next era of media includes investing in our employees to help them do their best work, and we’re just as committed to employee growth as we are to responsible media investment. WPP Media employees can tap into the global WPP Media &amp;amp; WPP networks to pursue their passions, grow their networks, and learn at the cutting edge of marketing and advertising. We have a variety of employee resource groups and host frequent in-office events showcasing team wins, sharing thought leadership, and celebrating holidays and milestone events. Our benefits include competitive medical, group retirement plans, vision, and dental insurance, significant paid time off, preferential partner discounts, and employee mental health awareness days.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WPP Media is an equal opportunity employer and considers applicants for all positions without discrimination or regard to particular characteristics. We are committed to fostering a culture of respect in which everyone feels they belong and has the same opportunities to progress in their careers.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We believe the best work happens when we&#39;re together, fostering creativity, collaboration, and connection. That&#39;s why we’ve adopted a hybrid approach, with teams in the office around four days a week. If you require accommodations or flexibility, please discuss this with the hiring team during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Please note this is a UK based role and requires individuals to have the right to work in this location&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please read our Privacy Notice (&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.wppmedia.com/pages/privacy-policy&quot;&gt;https://www.wppmedia.com/pages/privacy-policy)&lt;/a&gt; for more information on how we process the information you provide.&lt;/p&gt;
